{"id": "unknown-2026-09-12-008", "date": "2026-09-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "How Bangladesh’s yarn curbs exposed sharp industry fault lines", "content": "Bangladesh’s NBR has tightened duty-free 10–30 count cotton yarn imports under the bond facility for export-oriented readymade garment factories.\nSpinners say the move will lift demand for local yarn, revive mills, boost value addition, conserve foreign currency and support jobs.\nBGMEA and BKMEA warn bank guarantees may raise costs, disrupt shipments and weaken garment export competitiveness.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/how-bangladesh-s-yarn-curbs-exposed-sharp-industry-fault-lines-313408-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
